# Unix-only protect tests — focused Windows validation

## Source and scope

- Staging base: `migration/orca-faithful-import@53d8f8344f3f17f28766c7c880981147d3e128c6`.
- `crates/sandbox-providers/src/local/protect.rs` has the same blob (`cff47cb96368923b569edb478e5fd33415b23d1d)) in the pinned Orca source and FineCore staging.
- The Windows workspace log for this staging revision stops compiling tests at an unconditional `std::os::unix::fs::symlink` call. The test module also contains a POSIX `/workspace` path assertion and a `sh` helper.
- Applied `#[cfg(unix)]` to the two POSIX-only tests and their shell helper. Production code and portable tests are unchanged.

## Environment and results

- Windows, Rust/Cargo 1.99.1.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: PASS.
- `cargo test -p orca-harness-sandbox-providers local::protect::tests -- --test-threads=1`: PASS; 1 portable test passed, 0 failed, 2 Unix-only tests were excluded. The command compiled the crate's test targets; the prior Windows `E0433` compile error is absent.
- This is focused crate evidence only. The full Windows workspace suite was not rerun; Windows-specific runtime coverage of symlink protection remains unverified.
- Linux full tests and hosted CI remain pending, so no migration-wide or platform-wide gate is closed.

The limitation is preserved: the Unix path/symlink tests do not run on Windows, where this module's shell-based test is not portable.
